{"name":"Hot Magenta","hex":"#ff00cc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hot","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Hote."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Relating to heat and conditions which produce it.\n Having or giving off a high temperature.","Having or giving off a high temperature."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hot"},{"term":"magenta","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color which is close to the equal mixture of red and blue which is an additive secondary color but a subtractive primary color evoked by the combination of red and light blue."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having the color of fuchsia, fuchsine, light purple."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/magenta"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shades of magenta","blocks":[{"text":"The color magenta has notable tints and shades. These various colors are shown below."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Color_icon_magenta.svg/330px-Color_icon_magenta.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_magenta","wikidata":"Q17079435"},{"title":"Magenta","blocks":[{"text":"Magenta is a purplish-pink color. On color wheels of the RGB and CMYK color models, it is located directly midway between blue and red. It is one of the four colors of subtractive ink used in color printing by most color printers, also known as CMYK along with yellow, cyan, and black to make all the other colors and hues. The tone of magenta used in printing, printer's magenta, is redder than the magenta of the RGB (additive) model, the former being closer to rose."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Pink_swanboat_hosting_a_real_bird_on_its_head%2C_on_Shinobazu_Pond%2C_Ueno_Park%2C_Tokyo.jpg/330px-Pink_swanboat_hosting_a_real_bird_on_its_head%2C_on_Shinobazu_Pond%2C_Ueno_Park%2C_Tokyo.jpg?ut